  "what_this_is": "Cell B4b-rep (docs/readiness/2026-09-17-slurp-b4b-replicate-v2-preregistration.md): the REQUEST-IDENTICAL SAME-ROSTER REPLICATE of cell B4b, the date/time slot-contract revision (module M4b, slot store v2) on the sealed dual-store anchor, configs/baseline/slurp-native-anchor-slot-store-v2-train-fold-a-v2.json. Not one configured channel moves: the same arm speech-feature-query-native-tools, the same policy phase-native-candidates-review-revise-v1, the same full native episode with the Reviewer/Planner review loop on (max_revisions 1, reviewer max_iterations 3, program ceiling 11 contacts), the same Reviewer-only task-contract tool authority and Solver-only answer authority, the same model fragment (temperature 0, seed 20260913, max_tokens 512), the same dataset fragment and 1,080-row TRAIN Fold A roster, the same two knowledge stores at intent-boundaries-v1 and slot-contracts-v2 with their release and snapshot hashes, the same candidate supply contract, the same Perception retrieval geometry, the same phase material and instruction templates, the same phase_tools block, the same promoted EVO-FOLDS-V2 speech packets and the same resident geometry as cell B4b. Only the run, generation-attempt and native-fit identities and the WAVE R7 speech-feature identity strings are fresh, and the prepared first-phase supply is rebuilt because core.preparation.artifact_inputs binds the composed values (run and attempt ids included) and the SHA-256 of rails.kb_policy, rails.knowledge_provider, rails.phase_supply, rails.knowledge_stores and core.flight.runtime, two of which moved since B4b flew at 19ad05b4. NONE of those identities reaches a rendered request byte: core.model.transport validates the speech-feature identity strings and drops them, native contact-fit receipts are namespaced by the FIT run and attempt id, and the row-for-row envelope comparison of the preregistration section 3.1 proves the rendered request is byte-identical to cell B4b's on all 1,080 rows and all four declared phases. The factor under test is therefore batch composition under greedy decoding on this runtime and nothing else: llama-server at temperature 0 does not return bytes independent of how requests batch across slots, so a cell that changes nothing still moves the numbers, and the size of that movement is module M4b's own null -- the measurement the 2026-09-08 family rule requires before an admitted module may be frozen, and the obligation the provisional M4b harness-admission entry carries. Fold B is absent. The separate generation and native fit identities do not authorize contact; readiness is held until the coordinator pins the root decision receipt and flips it with scripts/flights/repin_cell.py.",
